import{_ as t,o,c as n,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const u=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Timeline events and the Notebook's name","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/timeline-events-episode.md","filePath":"records/timeline-events-episode.md"}`),a={name:"records/timeline-events-episode.md"};function d(r,e,i,h,c,l){return o(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="timeline-events-and-the-notebook-s-name" tabindex="-1">Timeline events and the Notebook&#39;s name <a class="header-anchor" href="#timeline-events-and-the-notebook-s-name" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Timeline events and the Notebook&#39;s name&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Updated 2026-11-01. The user asked for two things. Plugins should hand the timeline &quot;who did what, when&quot; as events, so the person&#39;s Notebook cells and Console commands appear on it. And they asked whether the Notebook should be renamed. In a Rho conversation they had asked &quot;可以在notebook 中演示一下ggplot2吗？&quot;, and the Agent made a Quarto document instead of using Rho&#39;s Notebook.</p><h2 id="the-notebook-s-name" tabindex="-1">The Notebook&#39;s name <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-notebook-s-name" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Notebook&#39;s name&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Observed.</strong> That conversation began on 2026-10-27, before Rho told its Agents about the Notebook (2026-10-30). In the turn, Claude Code with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash checked R, ggplot2, IRkernel and Quarto with Bash. It found Jupyter with only a Python kernel, wrote <code>ggplot2-demo.qmd</code> and rendered it. It never looked up <code>kernel.run</code>. The conversation&#39;s grant held <code>kernel.run</code>. The ACP adapter (<code>claude-agent-acp</code> 0.97.0) passes Rho&#39;s appended instructions when it loads a session as well as when it creates one, so the Notebook part was present.</p><p><strong>Reproduced.</strong> The question was asked with the person&#39;s exact words, the same model, Rho&#39;s appended instructions, Claude Code&#39;s native tools and Rho&#39;s MCP tools under the conversation profile (<code>work/notebook-name/headless.mjs</code>). Nothing asked for permission: Rho&#39;s tools, reads and listings ran, and other calls were refused and recorded.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>First Rho step</th><th>Cells run in the R session</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>New session</td><td><code>rho_index</code> for <code>kernel</code></td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>First message answered without the Notebook part, then resumed</td><td><code>rho_index</code> for <code>kernel</code></td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>As above, with the person&#39;s own Claude Code settings</td><td><code>rho_index</code> for <code>kernel</code></td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>New session with the sentence below</td><td><code>rho_index</code> for <code>kernel</code></td><td>10</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Every run used the shared R session; none looked for Jupyter or Quarto. Replaying the failed conversation&#39;s own history meant writing a copy of its transcript into <code>~/.claude/projects</code>. Claude Code&#39;s permission check refused that as transcript tampering, so the failure itself was not reproduced. A session whose earlier messages worked in other ways is the remaining difference.</p><p><strong>Decided.</strong> The Notebook keeps its name. The person says &quot;notebook&quot; because the page is called that, and Agents in new sessions took the word as Rho&#39;s sessions in every run. A rename would change the words on every screen without touching the case that failed. Agents started in Rho now read one more sentence: something asked for &quot;in the notebook&quot;, or in the R or Python session, means these sessions on Rho&#39;s Notebook page, not a Jupyter, Quarto or R Markdown notebook, unless a file is named. Whether it changes the outcome for a long, older conversation is not established.</p><h2 id="who-did-what-when" tabindex="-1">Who did what, when <a class="header-anchor" href="#who-did-what-when" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Who did what, when&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Before.</strong> The timelines drew only what conversations record. The person&#39;s cells and commands were absent. An Agent&#39;s own cells were absent too, because a <code>rho_call</code> to <code>kernel.run</code> is recorded as a project call, not a run.</p><p><strong>Changed.</strong></p><ul><li>Plugin contracts carry one event shape: who (<code>by</code>), what (<code>label</code>), where, when it began and ended, and how it ended (<code>running</code>, <code>done</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>stopped</code>, <code>unknown</code>). A plugin names its events read in <code>timeline</code>. Notebook 0.5.0 reads <code>kernel.events</code> and Console 0.3.0 reads <code>console.events</code>, newest first, without code or output.</li><li>Rho lists each plugin&#39;s <code>timeline</code> in the catalog, reads every one the tab may call, and places each event by principal. The person at this machine has a lane named You, above the conversations. An Agent started in Rho is known by its conversation&#39;s principal, so its cells join that conversation&#39;s lane. Anyone else shares a lane named Outside Rho. Pointing at a block says &quot;You ran summary(fit) · R&quot;, with Failed, Stopped or Outcome unknown when it applies.</li><li>The Overview&#39;s strip appears when only the person has worked, as What you did, and otherwise as What you and the Agent did.</li><li>A conversation&#39;s Studio draws its own Agent&#39;s events and the person&#39;s since it began, the same share its Notebook view shows. A replayed moment at one of them brings the Notebook or Commands view forward when the Studio has one.</li></ul><h2 id="runs" tabindex="-1">Runs <a class="header-anchor" href="#runs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Runs&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>work/timeline/episode.mjs</code> copied the person&#39;s Rho-Playground to <code>/tmp</code>, with its conversation and its Notebook cell. In the browser the person ran a failing cell, a working one and two commands. A caller holding an outside grant ran a cell, as an Agent outside Rho would. The Overview, the Graph and the conversation&#39;s Studio were then shown at 1440 px.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Pass</th><th>Observed</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Lanes You, the conversation and Outside Rho with the right events, and a tooltip naming the command. The 20 seconds of new work had about 10 px after a 4.7 h pause, beside a stretch of days</td><td>Each stretch first gets room for its steps (<code>stretchSizes</code>), then shares the rest by duration</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>The conversation&#39;s brand mark stood above its name: the global <code>.conversation</code> style matched the lane&#39;s class</td><td>The lane marks who it is with <code>data-who</code></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Four separate blocks in You with the failed cell outlined, the outside cell below, and the person&#39;s cells after the pause in Studio&#39;s side timeline. The outside cell was left out there</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Person only</td><td>A new project with two cells and a command shows What you did with one lane, with no page errors and no sideways scroll at 390 px</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="checks" tabindex="-1">Checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Checks&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Rho 267/269 in the ledger. A rerun showed its two misses: the MCP v2 test at its 30 s limit and the <code>.rho</code> cleanup race after a Console test. Each passes alone, MCP v2 in 23.9 s twice. Plugins 163/163, with new tests for both events reads. The pinned contracts export list gained the timeline names.</p><p>The graph, frontend and pages acceptances passed. agent-canvas failed where it clicked 10 px into Studio&#39;s side timeline. The click had depended on a cramped first stretch to land after the first read; with the new sizing it landed on the question, and an earlier step&#39;s check had been passing on an empty Studio. The acceptance now clicks the first read mark, passes 10/10, and its replay shows the data and script read then.</p><h2 id="left-open" tabindex="-1">Left open <a class="header-anchor" href="#left-open" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Left open&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>No Agent started in Rho ran cells in these browser runs, because its permission prompts are the person&#39;s to answer. Its cells in its conversation&#39;s lane are covered by unit tests only.</li><li>A replayed moment at the person&#39;s cell bringing the Notebook forward was not exercised.</li><li>Lane names are hidden at phone width, for conversations as before.</li><li>The Graph page still shows &quot;Nothing to draw yet&quot; without conversations, even when the person has worked.</li></ul>',21)])])}const w=t(a,[["render",d]]);export{u as __pageData,w as default};
